"icon-browser usage" is a notebook page
	<header level="1">
		Icon Browser
		<header>An icon browser shows every icon of a pack, to search through: clicking one copies the name that draws it.</>
	</>

	<!-- USAGE:  how to use it, where its icons come from, keyboard, accessibility. -->
	<section label="Using it">
		<markdown>
			Put one on a page, and it shows every icon of a pack Spell UI ships, ready to search.

			- `pack` is the pack it starts on: `fa7-free` (the default), `fa7-brands` or `fomantic`.
			  Its buttons switch to another.
			- `query` is what it starts searching for.
			- `address` opens it on the search and the pack the page's address names: `?q=bell&pack=fa7-brands`,
			  as `spell icon bell --open` writes it.
			- Click an icon to copy its name: the name `<ui-icon name>` and every `icon` attribute take.
		</>
		<markdown>
			```html
			<ui-icon-browser pack="fa7-brands" query="git"></ui-icon-browser>
			```
		</>
	</>

	<section label="Its icons">
		<markdown>
			It shows the pack's own icons, one tile per glyph, whatever packs the page has.

			- Each pack loads on its own, so browsing Fomantic changes nothing the page's other icons mean.
			- A tile shows the name `name` takes; its other names are in its tooltip.
			- A search matches names first (exact, then starting with what you typed, then holding it),
			  then Font Awesome's search terms: `mail` finds `envelope`.
			- The grid draws its first tiles, then more as you scroll near its end: each glyph is a file of its own.
		</>
	</>

	<section label="Keyboard">
		<markdown>
			- Tab moves through the pack buttons, the search box and the tiles.
			- Enter or Space on a tile copies its name.
		</>
	</>

	<section label="Accessibility">
		<markdown>
			- The pack switch is a group of buttons, named "Icon pack"; the one shown is selected.
			- The search box is named "Search icons".
			- The tiles are a list of buttons, each named for its icon.
			- The count and the copied note are status messages: a screen reader reads them as they change.
		</>
	</>
